.TH XUR.STD.CELL 7 "2026-11-19" "xur 0.1.3" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.cell \- shared mutable values
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
use std::cell;

let c = cell::new(0);
c.set(42);
io::println("{}", c.get());
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::cell
provides a
.B Cell
type for sharing mutable state across closures and threads.
A Cell wraps a single value that can be read and written through a
shared reference.
.PP
Cells are type-checked: a
.B Cell<int>
created with an integer will reject writes of other types.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B new(value) -> Cell
Create a new cell containing
.IR value .
.SH METHODS
.TP
.B get() -> Value
Read the current value.
.TP
.B set(value) -> ()
Replace the stored value. Errors if
.I value
has a different type than the cell was created with.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::cell;
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let counter = cell::new(0);

    let inc = fn() {
        counter.set(counter.get() + 1);
    };

    inc();
    inc();
    io::println("count: {}", counter.get());
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.sync (7)
